
docker use volumes to store data, like 
dify/docker/volumes/db/data-workflow-0.6.1/pgdata

in dify/docker/docker-compose.middleware.yaml
version: '3'
services:
  # The postgres database.
  db:
    image: postgres:15-alpine
    restart: always
    environment:
      # The password for the default postgres user.
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: difyai123456
      # The name of the default postgres database.
      POSTGRES_DB: dify
      # postgres data directory
      PGDATA: /var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata
      TZ: "GMT+8"
      PGTZ: "GMT+8"
    volumes:
      - ./volumes/db/data-workflow-0.6.1:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    ports:
      - "5432:5432"

if you want to reset database, you need to delete dify/docker/volumes/db
there is a Pycharm plugin called Database Navigator for check database
